            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0297" n="201" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">362.115 St 21/469: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-12-20T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                                1926—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>337. For Hill. H–110. Your H–200, December 17, 1926, and Department’s 330 of
                    December 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d121-f1"/></p>
                <p>Department advised that Standard Oil made payment of $400,000 December 20 to
                    National City Bank account Reparation Commission.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
